{
  "assembly_notes": "Manual car scissor jack. One rigid jack_base root carries the base pan and both lower pin lugs. The linkage is a real pinned rhombus expressed as two chains in the URDF tree, both REVOLUTE about +y: base -> lower_arm_0 (the single independent driver) -> end_block_0 (mimic -1, so the block stays level) -> upper_arm_0 (mimic +1) -> saddle_head (mimic -1, so the saddle stays level); and base -> lower_arm_1 (mimic -1) -> end_block_1 (mimic +1) -> upper_arm_1 (mimic +1), whose free end tracks the saddle pin exactly by symmetry and bears on it. Those mimic multipliers are what make the closed rhombus exact: the saddle rises straight up to 2*arm_len*sin(theta) with no sideways drift. The lead_screw is a REVOLUTE (+x) child of end_block_0 running through the bore of end_block_1, which is built as a real square tube so the shank passes through it with running clearance. Four component slots vary without touching the mechanism: saddle_head, base_style, drive_head and arm_style; arm_plate_count repeats the arm plates across the frame width. arm_len_m, frame_width_m and screw_radius_m are independent continuous parameters deriving lift height, waist span, pin stations, block bore, nut size and drive head size; palette is non-core.",
